#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
no_so_pipeline.py — Pure-Python INE QR Crypto Pipeline (Layers 1-9)
=====================================================================
Complete, self-contained implementation of the pc() crypto pipeline from
libPersonalCode.so, derived entirely by disassembling and translating the ARM64
NEON SIMD blocks.  No Unicorn / lief / capstone dependency at runtime.
No libPersonalCode.so dependency at runtime — all .rodata constants and
AES ciphertexts are hardcoded inline.

Architecture:
  - Six NEON SIMD blocks derive three AES keys + three AES IVs from .rodata constants.
  - Three AES-CBC-256 + three RSA public-key decrypt rounds peel away nested keys.
  - The final RSA key pair is used to decrypt the QR binary payload (buf2).
  - A CRC/bitstream decoder extracts biographical fields and the photo.

Requirements:
    pip install cryptography numpy Pillow zxing-cpp
    (optional) pip install pillow-heif   # for HEIC/HEIF photos

Usage:
    python3 no_so_pipeline.py <credential_image>   # JPG, PNG, HEIC
    python3 no_so_pipeline.py --qr-left <l.bin> --qr-right <r.bin>   # pre-extracted
"""

